          <Data name="Other info">
            <value>My background is in biophysics, with little overlap to vaccine development.

I have a strong interest and broad experience in data sharing in public health emergencies [1] as well as in open science more broadly [2] and in covering science and medicine-related topics via the Wikimedia ecosystem [3].

I would thus like to assist RaDVaC from those angles.

A good way to reach me is via https://twitter.com/EvoMRI .

Some pointers to relevant activities I was involved in:
[1]
- Open drug discovery for the Zika virus. https://doi.org/10.12688/f1000research.8013.1
- Progress in promoting data sharing in public health emergencies. https://dx.doi.org/10.2471/BLT.17.192096
- Fostering global data sharing. https://wellcomeopenresearch.org/articles/5-267/v1
[2]
- The transformative nature of transparency in research funding. https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.1002027
- Publishing the research process. https://doi.org/10.3897/rio.1.e7547
- Open science in practice. https://doi.org/10.3897/rio.7.e68595
[3]
- Wikipedia as a gateway to biomedical research. https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0190046
- Representing COVID-19 information in collaborative knowledge graphs: the case of Wikidata. http://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.4549834
- Developing a scalable framework for partnerships between health agencies and the Wikimedia ecosystem.  https://doi.org/10.3897/arphapreprints.e68129</value>
          </Data>
        </ExtendedData>
      </Placemark>
